@section('title')Notifications@endsection
@section('description')The panel messages after a change, on the profile, the forgot-password and reset pages, and its errors on forms and sign-in. Your own flash messages and toasts are not built yet.@endsection

@section('content')
  <h1>{{ $title }}</h1>
  <p>The panel tells the user what happened with a message, and with the errors on a form.</p>

  <h2>Flash messages</h2>
  <p>After a change, the panel redirects and shows one message above the content. The page it returns to depends on the change:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>After a create, update or delete of a resource, the panel redirects to the list: <code>Record created.</code>, <code>Changes saved.</code> or <code>Record deleted.</code></li>
    <li>On the profile, the panel redirects to the profile: <code>Profile saved.</code>, <code>Picture saved.</code>, <code>Picture removed.</code>, <code>Password changed. Other devices were signed out.</code>, or <code>Choose a PNG, JPEG or WebP picture of up to 1 MB.</code> when a picture is refused.</li>
    <li>On the forgot-password page, the panel redirects back to it with <code>If an account exists for that email, we have emailed a password reset link.</code>. The same message shows for every request.</li>
    <li>After a password reset, the panel redirects to the sign-in page with <code>Your password has been reset. Sign in with the new password.</code></li>
  </ul>
  <p>A message shows once, on the next page the user loads. It is kept in a signed cookie, so the server holds no state for it.</p>

  <h2>Form errors</h2>
  <p>A form that does not validate shows its messages under the fields, and keeps the values the user typed. See <a href="/docs/forms">Forms</a>.</p>

  <p>A value that clashes with a unique index, such as a second user with the same email, shows <code>Email is already taken.</code> under its field. See <a href="/docs/forms">Forms</a>.</p>

  <h2>Sign-in errors</h2>
  <p>A wrong email or password shows <code>The email or password is incorrect.</code> on the sign-in page. Too many attempts show <code>Too many sign-in attempts. Try again in N seconds.</code> with status 429. See <a href="/docs/panel">Panel</a>.</p>

  <h2>Expired forms</h2>
  <p>A form whose security token is missing or wrong shows the Page Expired page, with status 419. Reload the page and try again.</p>

  <h2>Server errors</h2>
  <p>A row that does not exist gets a 404 page. A database error gets a 500 page, and the error is logged, not shown to the user.</p>

  <h2>Not built yet</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your own messages.</strong> The panel sets these messages itself. An app cannot set a flash message in v1.</li>
    <li><strong>Toasts.</strong> Messages appear in the page and do not fade away.</li>
  </ul>
@endsection
